-- title:
--   Dedekind special fibre of the j-finite chart of X₀(M')
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K_0$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ which equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} \mathbb{Q} \to \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\mathbb{Q}$ generated by all quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_0(M')$ (of equal weight, with nonzero denominator). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra subring of $L$ with $L$ as fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\varpi \in A$ generate that maximal ideal; assume $K_0$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K_0$. Let $j_0 \in K_0$ be nonzero with image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot\jmath_{\mathrm{num}}$ of the modular invariant. Then the quotient of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K_0$ integral over $A[j_0]$, by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ is a Dedekind domain.
--
--   This identifies the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_0(M')$ over a discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $q$ prime to $M'$ as a Dedekind domain, the good-reduction statement underlying the analysis of the fibre at $q$. It feeds the description of the maximal ideals of that chart above $\varpi$ in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.existsUnique_prime_le_jChartFin_sub_mem_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_chartAlgFin_gamma0_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.existsUnique_prime_le_jChartFin_sub_mem_map_sup_span_eq_maximalIdeal_chartAlgFin_gamma0_of_not_dvd).
